+# Phase 2 milestone #29 — Storybook asset pipeline
+
+Repository: `~/code/contraption-lab`
+
+Coworking session: `s-20260814-0920-a29c`
+
+## Workflow
+
+- Do not commit or push `contraption-lab`.
+- Use the normal prom-resp review flow.
+- Preserve unrelated local changes and untracked files, including the owner’s
+  local `docs/ROADMAP.md` “German Shoutout” edit, `docs/reviews/`, and
+  `s-20260812-1003-c7d4-response.md`.
+- Read `AGENTS.md`, `docs/PHASE2_RECONCILIATION.md`, the reference-art manifest,
+  the Sunny Attic art bible, and relevant rendering/schema/validation/inventory/
+  contact-tag/headless/scene code before editing.
+
+## Goal
+
+Establish the production Sunny Attic Storybook asset/rendering pipeline without
+cementing the old POC Ball/Ramp/Block taxonomy into future Chapter-1 content.
+Keep existing generic behavioral mechanics where useful; do not redesign the
+whole gameplay model.
+
+## Requirements
+
+1. Storybook assets are visual/content identity only. Matter geometry remains
+   explicit deterministic gameplay geometry. Sprite dimensions or transparent
+   bounds must never silently define collision bodies. Existing Phaser primitives
+   remain usable fallback/debug rendering.
+2. Create the smallest general asset/rendering structure that lets Chapter-1
+   objects use approved Sunny Attic assets without a named `createX` renderer
+   for every object. Do not build a giant framework.
+3. Prove the structure with exactly `mattress` and `teapot`, using their
+   approved reference-art assets. They must exercise the new structure; do not
+   add their Chapter-1 gameplay mechanics or levels. Cat is out of scope.
+4. Replace `{ ball, bird, block, ramp }` inventory with the smallest keyed,
+   registry-compatible representation needed for future Chapter-1 objects.
+   Mechanically migrate all five puzzle JSON definitions with unchanged
+   semantics.
+5. Generalize closed POC tag/type assumptions only where required. Keep one
+   authoritative registry/set for practical compile-time keys/tags, runtime JSON
+   validation, registry lookup, and clear unknown-value rejection. Do not accept
+   arbitrary unchecked strings or build a large registry framework.
+6. Capture the `f37b74a` headless baseline. Existing reference/headless verdicts
+   and tick counts, including #28 dynamic Blocks, must be unchanged afterward.
+7. Do not redesign the five existing puzzles beyond mechanical schema migration.
+8. Use the approved Sunny Attic archive without altering reference originals;
+   runtime copies or processing must retain clear provenance.
+9. Do not implement Chapter-1 levels #30–#35, Cat mechanics, mattress bounce,
+   teapot redirect, dependencies, broad unrelated refactors, or cleanup of
+   unrelated files.
+
+## Validation and handoff
+
+- During implementation use focused checks only; before handoff run once:
+  `npm run typecheck`, `npm run lint`, `npm test`, `npm run build`, and
+  `git diff --check`.
+- Run only focused Playwright coverage for the #29 rendering/asset proof.
+- Inspect the patch for syntax, formatting, truncation, accidental empty files,
+  unrelated changes, and scope creep.
+- Write `~/code/prom-resp/s-20260814-0920-a29c-response.md` and generate
+  `~/code/prom-resp/s-20260814-0920-a29c-diff.patch`, containing only #29
+  changes. Stage and commit only those artifacts in prom-resp, pull --rebase
+  `origin main` if required, then push `origin main`.
+- Report architecture, the mattress/teapot proof, inventory/tag decisions,
+  rendering/physics separation, baseline vs after headless results, focused
+  Playwright and final validation results, diff-check result, changed files,
+  preserved/excluded unrelated files, no contraption-lab commit/push, and the
+  prom-resp commit/push result.
